    "text_synthesis": {
      "type": "Text",
      "props": {
        "text": "Kalshi is going full Bloomberg — clearinghouse, terminal, perps, art markets, legal wins. Regulatory capture is the moat and it's working; the more TradFi they get, the wider the gap for a permissionless play. Hyperliquid proved the validator oracle model works (3× volume, day one) but doesn't have user-created markets yet. The actual product gap nobody's filling: user-created + leveraged + validator-resolved + no KYC. Premu has 3 of 4. The regulatory window is open right now — CFTC green-lit, 3rd Circuit won, McCormick/Gillibrand providing legitimacy cover. The next mover who stitches Hyperliquid's oracle + Premu's creation model + Noise's attention layer is building the cockpit, not the observation deck. That's the coordination machine. Everything else is infrastructure for it."
